{"availability":"available","full":"PAIR-code/agent-trace-vis","name":"agent-trace-vis","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":4,"forks":1,"created":"2026-06-30T22:50:39Z","updated":"2026-10-16T23:41:26Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://agent-trace-vis.netlify.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T18:04:32.307Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T18:04:32.307Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T18:04:32.307Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T11:08:05.176Z","stars":4,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-16T07:13:43.971Z","stars":4,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-19T18:04:32.307Z","stars":4,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Visual tools for understanding AI agent reasoning traces. Built for researchers, engineers, and anyone trying to make sense of complex agentic behaviors.","As AI systems increasingly rely on multi-step reasoning and tool use, understanding what they actually do, and why, becomes critical. But most of this behavior is hidden: the implementation steps, tool calls, backtracking, and decision points that shape the final output. This project explores visual approaches to making these patterns legible, from structured agentic traces (where agents coordinate tools, sub-agents, and user interactions) to unstructured chain-of-thought reasoning (where we want to compare strategies across multiple rollouts of the same task). Our goal is to bridge the gap…"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/PAIR-code/agent-trace-vis/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9cba51d89269bae4afc2d0fe46b555f49bdfa0f67cc723edb969cf6c10c570af","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T11:08:05.277Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T18:04:32.410Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Visual tools for understanding AI agent reasoning traces. Built for researchers, engineers, and anyone trying to make sense of comple